  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under RMBCA Section 2.02, articles of incorporation must be filed with the state to legally create a corporation. This document includes the corporate name, authorized shares, registered agent, and incorporator information.
Wrong (A): Bylaws are internal governance documents adopted by the board under RMBCA Section 2.06. They are not filed with the state.
Wrong (B): An operating agreement governs LLCs, not corporations. Corporations are formed by filing articles of incorporation, not operating agreements.
