UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Sara''s initial tax basis is her $80,000 cash contribution plus her 40% share of the $200,000 nonrecourse liability ($80,000), totaling $160,000. Under IRC Sec. 752, a partner''s share of partnership liabilities increases basis. Nonrecourse liabilities are generally allocated by profit-sharing ratios.
Wrong (A): The $80,000 figure reflects only Sara''s cash contribution and ignores her allocable share of the $200,000 nonrecourse loan, which adds $80,000 to her basis.
Wrong (C): The $120,000 figure incorrectly calculates Sara''s share of the liability. Her 40% of $200,000 is $80,000, not $40,000, so the total basis is $160,000.
Wrong (D): The $280,000 figure overstates Sara''s basis by allocating the entire $200,000 liability to her rather than her 40% share ($80,000).$EXPL$
