-- Q2524: Business Structures [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Sec. 1, a sole proprietorship is not a separate tax entity and does not file a separate federal income tax return. All business income and deductions are reported on Schedule C of the owner''s Form 1040. This statement is incorrect, making it the right answer to the question.
Wrong (B): This statement is true. Business income is indeed reported on Schedule C of Form 1040, so it is not the incorrect statement the question asks for.
Wrong (C): This statement is true. A sole proprietor has unlimited personal liability for all business debts because the business is not a separate legal entity.
Wrong (D): This statement is true. Under IRC Sec. 1401, the owner pays self-employment tax on net business income reported on Schedule C.$EXPL$
