UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under RMBCA Section 10.03, amending the articles of incorporation is a fundamental change requiring shareholder approval, typically by a majority vote. This is because amendments alter the corporation''s foundational charter filed with the state.
Wrong (A): Declaring dividends is a board-level decision under RMBCA Section 6.40. It falls within the board''s business judgment and does not require shareholder approval.
Wrong (B): Hiring officers is a management function delegated to the board under RMBCA Section 8.40. Shareholders do not vote on officer appointments.
