-- Q2528: Business Structures [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Sec. 702(a), each partner must include in gross income their distributive share of partnership items regardless of whether any distribution is actually made. Dave''s 50% share of $120,000 equals $60,000, reportable on his individual return.
Wrong (A): Partnership income is taxed to partners in the year earned, not when withdrawn. The partnership is a pass-through entity under IRC Sec. 701, so Dave reports income regardless of distributions.
Wrong (B): Dave''s distributive share is not limited to his capital contribution. His 50% profit-sharing ratio determines the $60,000 income allocation.
Wrong (D): Dave reports only his 50% share, not the full partnership income. The remaining $60,000 is allocated to Ellen as her distributive share.$EXPL$
