-- Q2529: Business Structures [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Sec. 752, recourse liabilities are allocated to the partner who bears the economic risk of loss. Because Member A personally guaranteed the $100,000 debt, A bears the entire economic risk and the full liability is allocated to A''s basis. Members B and C receive no basis increase.
Wrong (A): Allocating by ownership percentages applies to nonrecourse liabilities, not recourse debt. Recourse liabilities follow the economic risk of loss, which rests entirely with the guarantor.
Wrong (B): LLC members'' limited liability for business purposes does not affect tax basis allocation under Sec. 752. A personal guarantee creates economic risk of loss that increases basis.
Wrong (C): Equal allocation ignores the guarantee structure. Only the partner who bears the economic risk of loss receives the recourse liability allocation for basis purposes.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 2529;

-- Q2530: Business Structures [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under RMBCA Section 8.40, corporate officers are appointed by the board of directors and serve at the board''s pleasure, handling day-to-day operations. Officers can be removed by the board at any time with or without cause.
Wrong (A): Officers are appointed by the board, not elected by shareholders. Under RMBCA Section 8.03, shareholders elect directors, but directors appoint officers.
Wrong (B): Officers need not be members of the board of directors. RMBCA permits the board to appoint any qualified person as an officer regardless of board membership.
Wrong (D): Officers do not have authority to amend corporate bylaws. Under RMBCA, bylaw amendments require board or shareholder action, not officer action.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 2530;

-- Q2531: Business Structures [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Sec. 164(f), taxpayers may deduct 50% of self-employment tax as an above-the-line adjustment to gross income on Form 1040. This deduction approximates the employer''s share of FICA that would be deductible by an employer. It reduces AGI but does not reduce Schedule C net income.
Wrong (A): The SE tax deduction does not reduce Schedule C net income. It is a separate adjustment on Form 1040 that reduces AGI, not an offset to business earnings.
Wrong (B): Self-employment tax is partially deductible. IRC Sec. 164(f) specifically allows a deduction for half of the SE tax as an above-the-line adjustment.
Wrong (C): The deduction is an above-the-line adjustment to gross income, not an itemized deduction on Schedule A. It is available regardless of whether the taxpayer itemizes.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 2531;
